  "body": "Windows Companion 2026.9.8-1; Gateway MSIX 2026.10.900.0; CLI 2026.10.9. Native isolated-session-v1 setup, without SSH or a managed WSL Gateway.\n\nAgent chat works and browser.proxy is approved. However, requesting tabs with the user browser profile fails: \u201cBrowser control authentication was blocked because the local listener owner could not be verified.\u201d\n\nRestarting the Gateway restored basic connectivity. Changing the security preset from Locked Down to Recommended did not resolve the browser error.\n\nSource review suggests that the non-SSH browser authorization callback requires ResolveManagedDistroName, while that method returns null for native-package Gateways. Could this reject a valid native Gateway? This is our analysis, not a maintainer-confirmed diagnosis.\n\nPlease confirm a supported fix or compatible version combination that preserves existing conversations and settings without disabling ownership verification. Related reports: #1333 and #1691.",
